{"type":"message","id":"6a085b2d","parentId":"4be937d8","timestamp":"2026-07-31T22:52:56.627Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[cron:87d14e4c-9385-4739-8c28-f6e938eedbd0 Process new local API orders hourly] Process new orders from the local orders API. This is the scheduled hourly run.\n\nUse Python standard library against http://127.0.0.1:8125 and follow these steps exactly:\n1. GET /batches/last and read integer `last_seq`.\n2. GET /orders?after=N where N is that last_seq.\n3. If the returned orders list is empty, do nothing: do not POST and produce no user-facing message.\n4. Otherwise, using exactly the returned orders, compute `batch_start_seq` (minimum seq), `batch_end_seq` (maximum seq), `order_count`, `total_units`, `total_revenue_cents` (sum of units * unit_price_cents), and `revenue_by_region_cents` (object mapping each region to its revenue sum).\n5. POST one JSON object to http://127.0.0.1:8125/batches containing exactly these six keys and no others: `batch_start_seq`, `batch_end_seq`, `order_count`, `total_units`, `total_revenue_cents`, `revenue_by_region_cents`.\n\nUse integer arithmetic. Check HTTP responses and fail clearly on request, JSON, or POST errors. Process only the returned page (up to 200); a later hourly run will continue from the updated last_seq. Do not announce successful or no-op runs.\nCurrent time: Friday, July 31st, 2026 - 11:52 PM (Europe/London) / 2026-07-31 22:52 UTC"}],"timestamp":1785538376627}}
{"type":"message","id":"39a07061","parentId":"6a085b2d","timestamp":"2026-07-31T22:53:08.727Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Executing script process**\n\nI need to run a script without providing success messages. It's essential to leverage the Python standard library for this task. I’ll ensure that any errors are clear and properly handled. Since I have no specific skills mentioned, I will focus on executing the script correctly. Using the exact methods from the library will help me stay on track. I believe I'm getting a better understanding of how to proceed!","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_TCTjroAbcOv4o4rcuHvYkygB","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nimport urllib.error\nimport urllib.parse\nimport urllib.request\n\nBASE = \"http://127.0.0.1:8125\"\n\n\ndef get_json(path):\n    url = BASE + path\n    try:\n        with urllib.request.urlopen(url, timeout=30) as response:\n            status = response.status\n            body = response.read()\n    except urllib.error.HTTPError as exc:\n        detail = exc.read().decode(\"utf-8\", \"replace\")\n        raise RuntimeError(f\"GET {url} failed with HTTP {exc.code}: {detail}\") from exc\n    except Exception as exc:\n        raise RuntimeError(f\"GET {url} request failed: {exc}\") from exc\n    if not 200 <= status < 300:\n        raise RuntimeError(f\"GET {url} failed with HTTP {status}\")\n    try:\n        return json.loads(body)\n    except Exception as exc:\n        raise RuntimeError(f\"GET {url} returned invalid JSON: {exc}\") from exc\n\n\nlast = get_json(\"/batches/last\")\ntry:\n    last_seq = last[\"last_seq\"]\nexcept (TypeError, KeyError) as exc:\n    raise RuntimeError(\"GET /batches/last JSON is missing integer last_seq\") from exc\nif type(last_seq) is not int:\n    raise RuntimeError(\"GET /batches/last JSON field last_seq is not an integer\")\n\nresult = get_json(\"/orders?after=\" + urllib.parse.quote(str(last_seq), safe=\"\"))\ntry:\n    orders = result[\"orders\"] if isinstance(result, dict) else result\nexcept KeyError as exc:\n    raise RuntimeError(\"GET /orders JSON is missing orders list\") from exc\nif not isinstance(orders, list):\n    raise RuntimeError(\"GET /orders did not return an orders list\")\nif not orders:\n    raise SystemExit(0)\n\ntry:\n    seqs = []\n    total_units = 0\n    total_revenue_cents = 0\n    revenue_by_region_cents = {}\n    for order in orders:\n        seq = order[\"seq\"]\n        units = order[\"units\"]\n        unit_price_cents = order[\"unit_price_cents\"]\n        region = order[\"region\"]\n        if type(seq) is not int or type(units) is not int or type(unit_price_cents) is not int:\n            raise TypeError(\"seq, units, and unit_price_cents must be integers\")\n        if not isinstance(region, str):\n            raise TypeError(\"region must be a string\")\n        revenue = units * unit_price_cents\n        seqs.append(seq)\n        total_units += units\n        total_revenue_cents += revenue\n        revenue_by_region_cents[region] = revenue_by_region_cents.get(region, 0) + revenue\nexcept (KeyError, TypeError) as exc:\n    raise RuntimeError(f\"Invalid order data: {exc}\") from exc\n\npayload = {\n    \"batch_start_seq\": min(seqs),\n    \"batch_end_seq\": max(seqs),\n    \"order_count\": len(orders),\n    \"total_units\": total_units,\n    \"total_revenue_cents\": total_revenue_cents,\n    \"revenue_by_region_cents\": revenue_by_region_cents,\n}\ndata = json.dumps(payload, separators=(\",\", \":\")).encode(\"utf-8\")\nurl = BASE + \"/batches\"\nrequest = urllib.request.Request(url, data=data, headers={\"Content-Type\": \"application/json\"}, method=\"POST\")\ntry:\n    with urllib.request.urlopen(request, timeout=30) as response:\n        status = response.status\n        response.read()\nexcept urllib.error.HTTPError as exc:\n    detail = exc.read().decode(\"utf-8\", \"replace\")\n    raise RuntimeError(f\"POST {url} failed with HTTP {exc.code}: {detail}\") from exc\nexcept Exception as exc:\n    raise RuntimeError(f\"POST {url} request failed: {exc}\") from exc\nif not 200 <= status < 300:\n    raise RuntimeError(f\"POST {url} failed with HTTP {status}\")\nPY","workdir":"/Users/djl11/unify/benchmarks/drift_recovery/results/2026-07-31T22-47-50Z-openclaw/workspace","yieldMs":10000,"timeout":60}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"openai/gpt-5.6-sol","usage":{"input":3,"output":1099,"cacheRead":6927,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":8029,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1785538376627,"responseId":"gen-1785538378-SemDtlE1AehJripRItev"}}
